Design choices:
  - 4 separate Drizzle queries instead of an aggregated CTE: Prisma's
    findUnique-with-includes was already 2 queries; the per-unit lesson fan-out
    is N+1 by design (preserves Prisma's parallel-friendly fetch shape) and
    matches what other migrated reading-advantage controllers do.
  - count() via separate aggregate query rather than COUNT(*) OVER() window:
    keeps the read pure and easy to test in isolation. studentCount and the
    students array are derived from the same junction, so consistency is the
    DB's job, not the controller's.
  - StandardsAlignment cast at the boundary: Drizzle text column \u2192 union type.
    Safe because the legacy Prisma enum check constraint still exists at the
    Postgres layer (migration 0013 preserves it).

